                    "value": "Yes"
                },
                {
                    "type": "DATA",
                    "value": "Most medicines for chronic conditions: percentage co-payment of 10% of the retail price up to a maximum amount of €4.24 per prescription item (updated annually in line with inflation)\n\nAll other medicines: \n- pensioners with an annual income < €100 000: 10% \n- pensioners with an annual income > €100 000: 60% \n- people covered by mutual funds (MUFACE, MUGEJU and ISFAS): 30% \n- all others with an annual income < €18 000: 40% \n- all others with an annual income €18 000–100 000: 50%\n- all others with an annual income > €100 000: 60% Ortho-prosthetic devices (e.g. supportive braces and splints, prostheses, wheelchairs, crutches and hearing aids):\n- pensioners with an annual income < €100 000: 10% \n- pensioners with an annual income > €100 000: 60% \n- people covered by mutual funds (MUFACE, MUGEJU and ISFAS): 30% \n- all others with an annual income < €18 000: 40% \n- all others with an annual income €18 000–100 000: 50% \n- all others with an annual income > €100 000: 60%\n\nA cap per item varies from €0 to €36 per item and is not linked to income"
                },
                {
                    "type": "DATA",
                    "value": "No"
                },
                {
                    "type": "DATA",
                    "value": "People (for ortho-prosthetic devices)\n\nIncome\n    • people receiving non-contributory pensions\n    • unemployed people who have exhausted their unemployment benefits\n\nHealth status\n    • people with toxic shock syndrome\n    • a very small number of people with disabilities (with further exemptions for people with disabilities in some regions)\n\nOther\n    • people requiring treatment due to occupational illness or injury\n\nServices\n\nProstheses for breasts and upper and lower limbs, wheelchairs and wheelchair accessories are exempt from co-payment"
                },
